# BEFORE FIX — evidence for WE-20260528-004
# Captured: 2026-05-29

## .env.example default

$ grep FRONTEND_BASE_URL easebot-backend/.env.example
FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

## Controller logic

easebot-backend/src/controllers/paymentController.ts:415
  const frontend = env('FRONTEND_BASE_URL')   // throws if unset

env() helper (line 59-63):
  function env(name: string): string {
    const v = process.env[name]
    if (!v) throw new Error(`missing env: ${name}`)
    return v
  }

## Curl reproduction (simulated — dev backend needs PayU/Firebase secrets to boot)

Assuming a dev who copied .env.example as-is:
  FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

$ curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/payment/return \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \
  -d 'status=success&txnid=test' -i | grep -i location

HTTP/1.1 302 Found
Location: http://localhost:8080/payment/failure?reason=bad_payload
              ^^^^ DEAD URL — Vite dev runs on :8081

$ curl -I http://localhost:8080
curl: (7) Failed to connect to localhost port 8080 after 0 ms: Connection refused

## Impact

Every developer who copies .env.example verbatim is broken on payment day-1:
  - Successful PayU sandbox txn → browser redirected to dead :8080 host
  - Failed PayU sandbox txn → same dead :8080 host
  - No frontend success/failure page reachable

Production was unaffected only if the deploy env sets FRONTEND_BASE_URL
explicitly. If a deploy ever forgot to set it, env() would throw in the
handler → 500, but startup still proceeded because validatePaymentConfig()
did not list FRONTEND_BASE_URL as required.
